like Afrikaans or whatever

00:07:11.063 --> 00:07:15.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, yeah, man,
it's a whole learning lesson

00:07:15.768 --> 00:07:18.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And is he speaking it
to the twins?

00:07:18.037 --> 00:07:19.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He is.
-All right.

00:07:19.205 --> 00:07:20.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they know like "cheese"
and "kaas,"

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:24.510
and they'll just say dog and doy
and goodbye and stuff.

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:26.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I love it.
You know, a lot of people are,

00:07:26.813 --> 00:07:28.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, "Do you want to know
what they're saying?"

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm, like, "No,
I want to take a break.

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:31.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] Right.
-Let them talk to each other

00:07:31.984 --> 00:07:34.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
You come at me if you need me.
You know where I'm at.

00:07:34.053 --> 00:07:35.922 size:84% position:42%
I'll be in the kitchen,
washing these spoons."

00:07:35.922 --> 00:07:37.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You were saying --
You know, and again,

00:07:37.256 --> 00:07:39.959
I think a lot of comedians, it's
been a really difficult year

00:07:39.959 --> 00:07:42.295
Again, you caught a break in
that you got your special out.

00:07:42.295 --> 00:07:45.364
But, you know, especially when
you're building a stand-up act

00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:46.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's so important
to have an audience.

00:07:46.466 --> 00:07:48.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Whereas, when you're doin

00:07:48.668 --> 00:07:50.603 size:84% position:42%
a half-baked monologue,
it's totally the same.

00:07:50.603 --> 00:07:53.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-But you -- I want to ask this

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:55.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I did do comedy
for a long time

00:07:55.308 --> 00:07:57.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
in front of Dutch audiences.
I find them to be

00:07:57.310 --> 00:08:01.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
a very fair audience
but a very honest audience

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:03.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You sound like you're married
to a Dutch person.

00:08:03.049 --> 00:08:05.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, they're horrible.
I'm just kidding!

00:08:05.151 --> 00:08:07.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look, no, Dutch people,
it's really funny.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:09.322 size:88% position:44%
Dutch people are sort of
like your family, right?

00:08:09.322 --> 00:08:14.360
So, you know, you can't make fun
of them, but, you know,

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:17.597
they can make fun of themselves,
but you can't make fun of them

00:08:17.597 --> 00:08:18.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
They get very offended.
-Gotcha.

00:08:18.965 --> 00:08:21.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But, um, you know,
funny is funny.

00:08:21.334 --> 00:08:22.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I feel like
if the world is laughing,

00:08:22.735 --> 00:08:24.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
then they'll laugh along.
So now they like it.

00:08:24.704 --> 00:08:27.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
But before, when I was working
my material out there,

00:08:27.373 --> 00:08:28.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
they didn't like it.
-Really?

00:08:28.975 --> 00:08:29.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But I --

00:08:29.876 --> 00:08:32.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're a very honest people
So, is that helpful?

00:08:32.778 --> 00:08:35.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you -- Does your husban
tell you when --

00:08:35.047 --> 00:08:37.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I'm sure he's a fa
of yours, but is he ever like,

00:08:37.583 --> 00:08:41.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
"This part is not funny"?
-Um, you know, he knows now.

00:08:41.087 --> 00:08:44.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
I told him, it's not what yo
say, it's how you say it.

00:08:44.657 --> 00:08:45.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it's not like,
"It's not funny."

00:08:45.658 --> 00:08:47.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's just like, "You could use
more work on that."

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:48.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-Do you know what I mean?

00:08:48.961 --> 00:08:51.564
-That's good.
-Yeah, but they're very blunt...

00:08:51.564 --> 00:08:52.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
-...even when you don't

00:08:52.565 --> 00:08:54.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
want to know.
-My wife is not Dutch,

00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:57.904
but she got a Dutch passport
so she could criticize me.

00:08:57.904 --> 00:08:59.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-I love that.

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:02.775
Do you know, 10 years ago, I did
a pilot with your brother?

00:09:02.775 --> 00:09:05.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do.
-In L.A. for the E! Network,

00:09:05.278 --> 00:09:07.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm still waiting to hea
if it gets picked up.

00:09:07.313 --> 00:09:09.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Oh, I hope it does!

00:09:09.415 --> 00:09:12.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congratulations on the second
season of "The Circle."

00:09:12.151 --> 00:09:14.320
Is that a fun show to do?
-Oh, it's so much fun.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:16.956
I mean, season one, it was like,
"What a wild idea.

00:09:16.956 --> 00:09:17.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're all gonna be
in quarantine.

00:09:17.957 --> 00:09:20.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
What's that like?!"
And now season two, we're like

00:09:20.593 --> 00:09:22.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Yeah, yeah, we got it.
We got it.

00:09:22.662 --> 00:09:24.163 line:92%
Let me just win this money."

00:09:24.163 --> 00:09:25.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's very fun.
-Well, that's cool.

00:09:25.932 --> 00:09:28.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations on that
and the special.

00:09:28.401 --> 00:09:32.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
And very excited, as I am
with all comedians I'm fans of

00:09:32.305 --> 00:09:34.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
to see you back
in front of people again.

00:09:34.607 --> 00:09:36.042 line:92%
It will be great for all of us

00:09:36.042 --> 00:09:38.177
Season two of "The Circle"
is streaming now on Netflix.

00:09:38.177 --> 00:09:39.445 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes!

